+# Volt body refinement from the new references — 2026-10-29
+
+The owner supplies new side and front-quarter references, then explicitly chooses a silver factory finish. V23 forms a stronger hollow through the door panels with a rising lower fold and fitted sill blades. Shallow paired bonnet channels catch the light. The front fascia now has two actual recessed vertical air-curtain openings with inset backs and four returns each, a broader light guide and a wider projecting splitter. Five broader aero wheel blades and body-coloured mirror caps follow the reference's design language. The factory body is silver `b8bbb9`, with charcoal `272f33` accents. Valid saved green or custom colours remain intact; other cars' defaults remain unchanged.
+
+[Compare native views before and after](evidence/volt-new-references-2026-10-29/before-after.html). The uploaded images are visual references; no image pixels, branding or external geometry are incorporated into production assets. This is original native geometry under the existing game materials and camera.
+
+Requirements: ERN01 sculpted door/sill and bonnet forms; ERN02 formed fascia openings/light guide/splitter; ERN03 broad aero wheels and fitted body-colour mirrors; ERN04 authorised silver factory finish with saved-colour preservation; R01 retain the lower cabin, 20 cm windshield advance, extended rear glass, complete door frames, painted quarter pillars, tyre articulation, handling and budgets; Q01 actual geometry/input checks, native evidence, refreshed assets and a scoped checkpoint.
+
+Runtime changes are `game/vehicle/electric_coachwork.gd`, `game/vehicle/electric_car_model.gd` and `game/vehicle/vehicle_livery.gd`. Tessellation is redistributed toward the sculpted side surfaces while staying within the established geometry budget. The first green preview exposed less clear lower seams; final side sampling and fitted seam offsets address that. The intermediate source and renders remain in this evidence directory. The prior fixed-quarter-glass removal is retained despite the small glass triangle visible in the new reference.
+
+Final body checks pass25/0; retained window/cabin18, bonnet40, rear shape24, continuity58, native model34, actual App58, racing23 and owned parsing pass. Visible full/simple geometry is118714/38324 within120000/45000; shadows total3673 triangles. All445 prepared meshes and52 pictures refresh. The unchanged construction fixture passes31/33 with only its two former minimum-roof-height failures. The new body regression casts rays through actual full/simple fascia triangles to verify the curtain backs are visible through openings rather than covered by paint; it also checks four-sided returns, complete door/window perimeters, quarter-glass removal, unchanged other-car defaults and exact preservation of valid saved green/custom colours. Existing focused bonnet, rear shape, continuity, window/cabin, native model and actual Garage/race checks remain separate. [Actual results and limitations](evidence/volt-new-references-2026-10-29/report.json) and [exact commands/exits](evidence/volt-new-references-2026-10-29/commands.json) record what was run. The inherited construction fixture's former minimum roof height is retained rather than weakened; its two obsolete height failures remain explicit.
+
+V23 prepared meshes, five shadows, the Volt Garage template and 52 native Garage/header/news/livery pictures refresh. Final clean/synthetic-wear views cover both sides, front, hood, pillars and rear on both desktop renderers. The before comparison uses the archived v22 native views at the same camera settings. Existing build identities and concurrent work are retained. Historical v22 assets and current car configurations are checked for preservation.
+
+[Review patch](evidence/volt-new-references-2026-10-29/task.patch) and [forward/reverse proof and hashes](evidence/volt-new-references-2026-10-29/checkpoint.json). The patch uses exact task-start source snapshots and retains concurrent entries in shared manifest baselines. It does not stage or modify the shared Git index.
+
+Reload/rebuild and owner appearance acceptance remain. Existing saved custom colours are preserved. No physical-device query/test, APK, owner-save/live/backend mutation, deployment or owner-process restart was performed. No aerodynamic improvement, phone frame-rate, exact photograph match or full-project parser pass is claimed. Desktop App hitches remain a separate limitation.
